Z||000001||Oreif||11-25-2000||09:44 PM||||I bought mine from Auto Zone. About same price as Carparts.com and Wrenchhead.com.<BR>Get the MOOG brand. They have slotted upper ball joints so you can get perfect alignment.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||11-25-2000||11:33 PM||||simply shop the diferant parts stores & online for Moog parts. It's been my experience that online and most of the chain stores are about the same price wise. Don't forget to ad in any shipping $ by online places when you figure price.||||reg||1
Z||000003||KissMySSFiero||11-25-2000||11:58 PM||||Ive found them at Autozone here in florida.  only looked for the 88's  they have them in stock from what they told me.  who knows if they looked it up right.  but they were for around $30 for the lowers.  thats one of the fixes im gonna do in the next month.  Has anyone found upper ball joints for the 88's?  if so where, how much,  and whats the availability?   TIA<BR>JOEJOE||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfiero||11-26-2000||12:17 AM||||Go to the Fiero Store for '88 upper ball joints (www.fierostore.com).  They're about $60 each.......well worth it (get them while you can).  You must grind the rivets off to remove the old ball joint.....new ones come with bolts and nuts in lieu of rivets.<BR> <BR>I believe Tim at Fiero Parts & Appraisals has them too.  (e-mail at tim@fieroparts.com).<P><p>[This message has been edited by mrfiero (edited 11-26-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Bob Englert||11-26-2000||09:38 AM||||I recently bought lower ball joints for my 87 GT's at AutoZone for $15 each!  They are McQuay Norris brand.  I bought Moog slotted upper ball joints from Wrenchead.com.<P><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000006||Will||11-26-2000||10:00 AM||||I also bought McQuay-Norris ball joints from Autozone. They are cheap, but they come with a liftetime guarantee. This means free ball joints for as long as you save the receipt! Even if they only last 30k mi, the next set is free.<P>     The McQuay-Norris upper joints have slotted bolt holes for camber adjustment.<BR>||||reg||1
